## 5. Threat-model questionnaire

1. Miner-visible surface: `fixtures/input.json` fields (task names, metric name and parameters), the public train split, `transform.json`. None of these reveal hidden rows or labels.
2. Seed leverage: no. Hidden rows are baked into the referee image, which is private; nothing is derived from the seed.
3. Degenerate submissions: {% if adversarial %}measured, see item 9.{% else %}a constant or random score gives recall close to the false-alarm budget (≈0) and cannot place.{% endif %}
4. Baseline resubmission: scores exactly the baseline, below any leader by the 1% margin.
5. Metric gaming: the metric is computed by the referee on hidden rows with fixed thresholds; batch order is fixed and labels never leave the referee.
6. Malicious responses: the referee validates shape and finiteness of every score batch; a bad batch scores 0 for those rows and is logged to `trace.jsonl`.
7. Profitable failure: any fault scores 0 for the affected rows; a crashed or unhealthy player scores 0 overall (`terminal_reason: player_error`).
8. Aggregation integrity: fixed row count; missing scores count as 0; {% if money_metric %}the metric is bounded by the holdout's fraud amount per day.{% else %}the metric is bounded in [0, 1].{% endif %}
9. Adversarial results: {% if adversarial %}run through the local referee on {{ adversarial_date }} (same images and Docker flow as the solvers). "Clearly below" means more than {{ adversarial_margin }} under the first model's {{ adversarial_baseline }} on the private holdout.

   | Submission | What it returns | Private holdout | Share of first model | Clearly below |
   |---|---|---|---|---|
{% for r in adversarial %}   | {{ r.name }} | {{ r.description }} | {{ r.score_text }}{% if not r.ok %} ({{ r.error }}){% endif %} | {{ r.share_text }} | {{ "yes" if r.below else "**NO**" }} |
{% endfor %}{% for r in adversarial if r.note %}
